7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402812} {:answer/id #uuid "4f7fabcd-36ae-58b0-87d4-d8ecadab32be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402813} {:answer/id #uuid "21da0e63-7d44-5e1d-a482-ba5640f5bd5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402814} {:answer/id #uuid "4ef29f12-1148-5d1b-91ab-01ba28b7b9ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402815}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0a355126-1182-5b56-87b6-9e46cb5cc71a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402811} :answer-field/id #uuid "3bbaa81d-9156-5f56-9880-e18958600dcc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402810}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "59f14d04-9b7d-5b14-8363-a42027c3b11c" :question/math-academy-id "q-42374" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 & 1 & 7 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 \\\\ -0 & 6\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statement are true regarding the matrices $A,B,$ and $C?$\n\nI. The product $AB$ is well defined\nII. The product $BA$ is well defined\nIII. The product $AC$ is well defined" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $A$ is a $4\\times 2$ matrix, $B$ is a $2\\times 4$ matrix, and $C$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nThere are $2$ columns in $A$ and $2$ rows in $B.$ Since the number of columns in $A$ equals the number of rows in $B,$ the matrices $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{A}_{4\\times \\boxed{\\text{2}}}{\\times }_{✓}{B}_{\\boxed{\\text{2}}\\times 4}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $4$ columns in $B$ and $4$ rows in $A.$ Since the number of columns in $B$ equals the number of rows in $A,$ the matrices $B$ and $A$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{B}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{4}}}{\\times }_{✓}{A}_{\\boxed{\\text{4}}\\times 2}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $2$ columns in $A$ and $2$ rows in $C.$ Since the number of columns in $A$ equals the number of rows in $C,$ the matrices $A$ and $C$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{A}_{4\\times \\boxed{\\text{2}}}{\\times }_{✓}{C}_{\\boxed{\\text{2}}\\times 2}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that all three statements are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101465 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100926 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b6e5e228-fa65-531d-a8da-e444079bd9d8" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Convergent Series Using Multiple Convergence Tests" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050498 :topic/math-academy-id 1172 :topic/title "Selecting Procedures for Analyzing Infinite Series"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8fbe892a-5add-5ca7-9040-2ec034a861e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099952} {:answer/id #uuid "c22a72c1-3740-5f29-b88d-c860f8cda74e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099953} {:answer/id #uuid "eb0ec8a2-0ec3-51b8-afde-c78ae0b471d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099954} {:answer/id #uuid "fd1f62d0-6ba0-5e14-868f-6d1c54e7e69a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :